---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteSettings } from '../lib/site';
import { amazonDisclosure } from '../lib/affiliate';
const { contact, production, privacyHost, privacyLogging, adsenseClient, amazonTag } = siteSettings();
const ads = production && Boolean(adsenseClient);
---
<Layout title="Privacy — Who Goes First?" description={ads ? 'Player names stay on your device. Learn about optional group memory, sharing, advertising, analytics, and your privacy choices.' : 'Player names stay on your device. Learn about optional group memory, sharing, and your Google Analytics choice.'}><div class="content-page prose"><h1>Privacy</h1><p class="lede">The picker runs on your device. Player names and results are not sent to a server.</p><h2>What this version stores</h2><p>Preferences use your browser’s local storage under <code>wgf:preferences:v1</code>: reveal choice, sound and motion settings, input mode, and a schema version. Names, seat order, and stable player IDs are saved only if you turn on “Remember this group.” We don’t store results or a history of picks.</p><p>Your light or dark appearance is saved separately under <code>wgf:theme</code>. If storage is blocked, the appearance switch still works for the current page.</p><p>Saved information stays until you forget it or clear this site’s browser data. Under Preferences, “Forget this group” clears the roster and returns to four seats. “Reset settings” resets preferences and stops remembering the current group. If storage is blocked, the picker works in memory and explains that changes may not persist.</p><h2>What leaves your device</h2><p>Loading a public website sends ordinary connection information, such as your IP address and requested page, to its host. {production ? <>The hosting provider is {privacyHost}. {privacyLogging}</> : 'This local version has no public hosting service configured. A public release must identify its host and review that host’s logging settings.'}</p>
{ads ? <>
<h2>Advertising</h2><p>Pages other than the picker show ads from Google AdSense. The picker, its method pages, and error pages have no ads. Google and its partners may use cookies and device identifiers to show, measure, and personalize ads, and to prevent fraud. Player names, group settings, and picks are never sent to Google. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noreferrer">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
<h2>Analytics</h2><p>Google Analytics receives a page address without search parameters, the page title, and basic device information. Google may use analytics cookies to recognize repeat visits. We use page views to understand site traffic. Automatic form, site search, click, scroll, video, and download tracking is off, and Google signals are disabled.</p>
<h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2><p>In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland, Google’s consent message asks before ads or analytics use cookies. Until you answer, those tags run without cookies. Elsewhere, ads and analytics start on page load.</p><p><button type="button" class="footer-action" data-consent-open>Change consent choices</button> (shown where Google’s consent message applies)</p><p><button type="button" class="footer-action" data-analytics-off>Turn off analytics on this device</button> <span data-analytics-status aria-live="polite"></span></p><p>You can turn off personalized ads across Google at <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noreferrer">My Ad Center</a>, or visit <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noreferrer">aboutads.info</a> and <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noreferrer">youronlinechoices.eu</a>. Browser settings can also clear site data.</p>
</> : production ? <><h2>Optional analytics</h2><p>Google Analytics loads only after you choose “Allow analytics.” It receives a page address without search parameters, the page title, and basic device information. Google may use analytics cookies to recognize repeat visits. We use page views to understand site traffic. Automatic form, site search, click, scroll, video, and download tracking is off. Player names, group settings, and picks are not sent.</p><p>Your choice is saved on this device under <code>wgf:analytics-choice:v1</code>. Use “Analytics choices” in the footer to change it. Choosing “No thanks” after allowing stops future collection and clears this site’s Google Analytics cookies. Browser settings can also clear site data.</p></> : <p>No analytics or advertising scripts run in this local preview.</p>}
{amazonTag && <><h2>Affiliate links</h2><p>{amazonDisclosure} Game pages link to Amazon search results for that game. The link contains the game name and our affiliate tag, nothing about you or your group. Amazon’s own privacy notice applies once you follow it. Affiliate links never influence which rules we publish or what they say.</p></>}
<p>Game searches are filtered on your device. The query and directory filter are kept in the page’s URL fragment so Back, reload and bookmarks can restore them. Copied page addresses and browser history can include them; they are not added to page requests. Publisher source links open an external website only when you follow them; that website has its own privacy practices. There are no {ads ? '' : 'ads, '}AI calls, accounts, or session recording.</p><h2>Sharing</h2><p>“Share” shares or copies a clean link. It removes query strings and fragments and includes no names, group settings, or winner. Your browser or operating system handles its own sharing interface.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>{contact ? <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>Contact the owner</a> : 'An owner contact address and public hosting details must be added before launch.'}</p><p class="small muted">Implementation policy · 26 September 2026.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/">Back to the picker</a></div></Layout>
